There is one rather significant difference:  at present, the weak
point in most extortion/kidnapping schemes is collecting payment
without getting caught.  Digital cash makes that problem somewhat 
less forbidding.  The reason kidnappers generally ask for CASH, 
in spite of the fact that physically collecting the cash is tactically
very dangerous, is because once collected it affords maximal privacy
and untraceability.  Digital cash has the same privacy/untraceability
features as does cash, but can be collected virtually instead of 
physically.  Therein lies the difference, and the danger.

