Digital cash can be traced if the payer and the bank conspire.

Observe the protocol. The payer blinds a random number, sends it to
the bank, which signs it, and the payer unblinds it. The cash is
handed to someone, where it is then turned into the bank. If the payer
tells the bank what the number he generated is, the bank can wait for
it. 

> Caveat: Do Not, I repeat, Do Not construe this argument as an indication that
>         I am in any way against making crypto widely available.  I do think
>         we need to (as DDFr points out) address the possible arguements
