I agree that cryptography has problems, but I suspect that none of
them are terribly new. Criminals could always conspire in private by
being smart enough not to use phones, anonymous letters could always
be sent, etc. The difference here is really the fact that crypto makes
telecommunications secure, thus permitting people to virtually
relocate overseas. Other than that, nothing about it is really a new
wrinkle -- its just a matter of being better, faster, stronger, etc,
than the old methods. 

