Which is why the extortionist would launder the money through his crime
organization.  In fact, money laundering would become an even more important
activity of such organizations. Not only would they use money laundering
for their internal operations, they would market the service to outsiders.

Money laundering digital cash would be done by exchanging the dirty cash for
clean cash--at a discount, of course.  The dirty cash is then reintroduced
into the banking system after some number of anonymous, untraceable transactions.

This works because digital cash can be exchanged (and verified) without approval 
or knowledge of the authorities.  The first guy to deposit dirty cash into a
